 ## Queue and Tickets
 
+### Queue
+
+A **queue** belongs to one entity (`queues.entity_id`). Attributes: `name`, `slug` (unique per `(entity_id, slug)`), `is_active`, `labels_i18n`.
+
+**Lifecycle (domain actions `App\Actions\CreateQueue` / `UpdateQueue`, owner/admin only):**
+
+- **Create:** name is trimmed, 1–255 chars; slug defaults to `Str::slug(name)` ("Atendimento Geral" → `atendimento-geral`) and an explicit slug is also slugified; new queues are active. The same slug may exist in another entity. A duplicate within the entity is a `ValidationException` (including a race hitting the DB unique index, which is mapped — never a raw `QueryException`).
+- **Update:** any combination of new name, new slug and active flag (nullable parameters; `null` means "leave unchanged"). Keeping the queue's own slug is fine; taking another queue's slug is a `ValidationException`.
+- **No hard delete.** Deactivation (`is_active = false`) retires a queue: its tickets are preserved, and issuing (`IssueTicket`) or calling (`CallNextTicket`, `Ticket::call()`) on it keeps failing with `InactiveQueueException`.
+- Employees, members of other entities and non-members get `AuthorizationException`; nothing is written.
+
+**Per-queue access grants (`queue_access`, action `App\Actions\SetQueueAccess`):**
+
+- Join table `(entity_membership_id, queue_id)` with `permissions` (JSON array of strings); the only permission today is `call` (`App\Enums\QueuePermission`).
+- A manager (owner/admin of the queue's entity) sets the permissions of a membership on a queue: a non-empty list upserts the row; an empty list revokes (deletes) it. Unknown strings or non-string entries → `ValidationException`, nothing stored. Membership and queue of different entities → `ValidationException`. Non-managers (including an employee granting themselves) → `AuthorizationException`.
+- Grant logs `queue.access.granted` and revoke logs `queue.access.revoked` on the `audit` channel, both with `actor_id`, `queue_id` and `entity_membership_id`. No revoke is logged when there was no row to delete.
+
+**Authorization policy (`App\Policies\QueuePolicy`, single source of truth):**
+
+| Ability | Rule |
+| ------- | ---- |
+| `create` (entity as argument) | Owner/admin of that entity. |
+| `update`, `manageAccess` | Owner/admin of the queue's entity. |
+| `call` | Owner/admin always (no grant row needed); employee only with a `queue_access` row for **that** queue whose `permissions` array contains `call` (corrupted non-array denies); everyone else denied. |
+
+Both call paths enforce `call`: `CallNextTicket` authorizes after locking the queue and checking it is active (`AuthorizationException`, no ticket changes, every call mode); `Ticket::call()` locks, rejects inactive queues with `InactiveQueueException`, then authorizes (`AuthorizationException`, even when the ticket was already called), then the "only waiting tickets" `LogicException`.
+
 ### Ticket
 
 Unit of service in the queue. It is **single-use** and receives **one single call** — all data is immutable after issuance, except `status`, `called_at` and `called_by_user_id` (filled when called). Attributes:
